### Silero VAD, GGML conversion (ggml-org)

The `streaming` feature's utterance-boundary detection runs Silero VAD through whisper.cpp's own
built-in support — a second, separate model file the operator supplies, not shipped in this
repository and not fetched by `scripts/fetch-model.sh`, which only knows the Whisper ladder
above. The GGML conversion is published by `ggml-org` (whisper.cpp's own maintainers) as
`ggml-silero-v5.1.2.bin` in the `whisper-vad` repository on Hugging Face; the original Silero VAD
model is MIT-licensed by the Silero Team (`snakers4/silero-vad`).

Its checksum is not recorded here yet: unlike the Whisper ladder, nothing in this repository
downloads or verifies this file automatically today, so a checksum written down before the file
is actually fetched and hashed would be an unverified figure presented as a real one. Record it,
in this same form (file name, origin, SHA-256), the first time something in this project actually
fetches and checks the file — not before.

## Rust dependencies

Recorded by Cargo, not restated here. `cargo tree` and `cargo license`
give the current answer; a copy in this file would be stale within a
release.

The one dependency worth naming is `whisper-rs`, which builds
whisper.cpp — MIT, by Georgi Gerganov and contributors. It is why this
project needs a C++ toolchain and edge-ear does not.
